## 1. Welcome to BrightPath!

Dear New Team Member,

Congratulations on joining BrightPath Analytics! We're excited to have you on the team. This guide walks you through your first 90 days at BrightPath, including key tasks, people to meet, and learning milestones. Use this as your roadmap to get up to speed, build relationships, and start making an impact.

Your success is our priority. If at any point you feel confused, unsupported, or need clarification, please reach out to your manager or your assigned buddy—there are no silly questions!

---

## 2. Before Day 1: Pre-Joining Checklist

You should have received a welcome email from HR. If you haven't, reach out immediately to **hr@brightpath.com**. Before your start date, please:

- [ ] Review and sign your offer letter and employment contract (signed copies submitted to HR)
- [ ] Submit required documents:
  - PAN Card (Permanent Account Number)
  - Aadhaar Card or passport copy
  - Bank account details (for salary transfer)
  - Address proof
- [ ] Share emergency contact information via the HR onboarding portal
- [ ] Review the welcome email for your:
  - Reporting manager's name
  - Start date and time
  - Office location or remote work setup instructions
  - Dress code reminder
  - IT setup instructions (if applicable)

---

## 3. Day 1 Checklist: Your First Day

**Arrival (9:30 a.m. or as specified in welcome email)**

- [ ] Arrive at the office or log in for your remote onboarding (exact location and video link will be in your welcome email)
- [ ] Meet your manager or the HR representative who will greet you

**Office Setup (if onsite)**

- [ ] Collect your laptop, access card, and desk
- [ ] Collect your phone (if issued), chargers, and any other equipment
- [ ] Get WiFi credentials and initial login details for your laptop

**Remote Setup (if working from home)**

- [ ] Receive shipping confirmation and tracking for your laptop and equipment
- [ ] Once laptop arrives, follow the setup guide emailed to you
- [ ] Test your internet connection and camera/microphone before your first day

**System and Account Setup**

- [ ] HR will provide your email credentials and initial passwords (change all passwords immediately)
- [ ] Set up your email and add BrightPath email signature
- [ ] Download and install approved tools:
  - Slack (communication)
  - Google Workspace or Microsoft Office (documents)
  - Project management tools (Jira, Asana, or similar—your manager will specify)
  - VPN (if required for your role)
- [ ] Set up multi-factor authentication (MFA) on all accounts for security

**Mandatory Compliance Training (Day 1)**

- [ ] Complete "Welcome to BrightPath" onboarding module in the HR portal
- [ ] Watch company overview video (5 min)
- [ ] Complete mandatory compliance trainings:
  - Code of Conduct and Workplace Behavior (10 min)
  - Anti-Harassment and Anti-Bullying Policy (15 min)
  - Data Protection and Information Security (20 min)
  - Health and Safety Basics (5 min)
- [ ] Download and review the Employee Handbook (provided as PDF)
- [ ] Submit acknowledgment form in the HR portal confirming you've read and understood policies

**Introductions**

- [ ] Meet your manager for 30–45 minutes to discuss:
  - Your role, responsibilities, and immediate priorities
  - Team structure and how your role fits
  - Expectations for the first 30 days
  - Answers to any immediate questions
- [ ] Meet your assigned buddy (a peer from your team or a neighboring team)
- [ ] Quick 10-minute meet-and-greet with your team
- [ ] Grab coffee or lunch with your manager or buddy (informal, to break the ice)

**Administrative Tasks**

- [ ] Complete HR portal profile:
  - Upload your photo
  - Add emergency contact information (if not done pre-joining)
  - Authorize deductions (insurance, retirement fund, etc.)
- [ ] Review benefit documents (health insurance, provident fund, leave policies)
- [ ] Download and read the first 2 sections of the Employee Handbook

**End of Day 1**

- [ ] Confirm you can access email, Slack, and core tools
- [ ] Set up automatic out-of-office if needed
- [ ] Go home and rest! You've had a full day.

