## 4. Week 1 Checklist: Settling In

**Knowledge and Culture Building**

- [ ] Read the complete Employee Handbook and sign the digital acknowledgment form in the HR portal
- [ ] Review the "Company Values and Culture" section and understand the core values
- [ ] Watch recorded team introductions or attend live team meetings
- [ ] Attend the company all-hands meeting (if one occurs this week)
- [ ] Shadow at least one client call, internal demo, or customer interaction relevant to your role

**Team Integration**

- [ ] Meet your assigned buddy regularly (daily check-ins for the first week)
- [ ] Attend team stand-up, planning, or regular sync meetings
- [ ] Clarify your role's responsibilities with your manager and document them
- [ ] Ask your buddy or manager for a tour of the office (if onsite) or virtual tour of systems
- [ ] Find out where to get coffee, lunch, and any other daily essentials

**Learning and Resources**

- [ ] Access the internal knowledge base and wiki (your buddy can help)
- [ ] Review key documents relevant to your role:
  - Product overview (marketing materials or internal wiki)
  - Org structure (who's who and what they do)
  - Team processes and workflows (how work gets done in your team)
- [ ] Download any apps or tools specific to your role

**Goal Setting**

- [ ] Meet with your manager to discuss and document your first 30-day goals (3–5 specific, achievable goals)
- [ ] Add these goals to your performance tracking tool (e.g., 15Five, Lattice, or spreadsheet)
- [ ] Confirm success criteria and how progress will be measured

**Administrative**

- [ ] Confirm that all setup and access is working correctly
- [ ] Ask HR about benefits enrollment (health insurance choice, provident fund setup, etc.)
- [ ] Join any team Slack channels or mailing lists relevant to your role

**Week 1 Reflection**

- [ ] By Friday, jot down any questions or concerns you have
- [ ] Have a brief check-in with your manager: "How is your first week going? Any blockers?"

