## 5. First 30 Days: Making Your Mark

**Focus Area 1: Foundational Learning**

- [ ] Complete all mandatory compliance trainings (data protection, security, anti-harassment, etc.) if not done on Day 1
- [ ] Complete role-specific orientation trainings provided by your team
- [ ] Review and understand the standard operating procedures (SOPs) relevant to your team
- [ ] Learn the basic workflows and how to execute them (don't worry about speed yet)

**Focus Area 2: Key Relationships**

- [ ] Schedule 1:1 meetings with your manager weekly (minimum 30 min each)
- [ ] Schedule "coffee chats" or intro calls with 5–7 key cross-functional partners (sales, engineering, support, etc.)
- [ ] Attend team meetings and meet as many team members as possible
- [ ] Build rapport with your buddy and other onboardees (if joining at the same time)

**Focus Area 3: Quick Wins**

- [ ] Volunteer for or be assigned at least one small, well-scoped task (2–3 days of work)
- [ ] Execute the task end-to-end: understand requirements, implement, test, communicate status, and deliver
- [ ] Get feedback from your manager on the outcome, your approach, and areas for improvement

**Focus Area 4: Product and Customer Knowledge**

- [ ] Use the company's own product (for 30–60 minutes) to understand core features
- [ ] Read 2–3 customer case studies or success stories
- [ ] Understand your company's value proposition (why do customers choose BrightPath?)
- [ ] Listen to at least one customer call or support ticket (with permission)

**Focus Area 5: Documentation and Accountability**

- [ ] Document questions and learnings in a private Notion, OneNote, or Google Doc
- [ ] Identify gaps in onboarding or processes (you'll see things as a new person that veterans miss)
- [ ] Share feedback with your manager on what helped you and what didn't
- [ ] By day 20, ask your manager to review your progress against your 30-day goals

**Week 2 Checkpoint**

- [ ] Are you finding your way around (physically and virtually)?
- [ ] Do you understand your role and your first priorities?
- [ ] Are you comfortable asking questions and reaching out for help?
- [ ] Any concerns or blockers? Raise them with your manager now.

**Week 3 Checkpoint**

- [ ] Are you picking up the basics of the role?
- [ ] Are you starting to understand the team's priorities and how you contribute?
- [ ] Mid-task check-in with your manager on your first deliverable.

**Week 4 Checkpoint (30-Day Review)**

- [ ] Review your 30-day goals with your manager: Have you achieved them? What was the quality of work?
- [ ] Assess your own performance: What went well? What was hard? What do you want to improve?
- [ ] Take a survey about the onboarding experience (links will be sent by HR)
- [ ] Celebrate! You've completed your first month.

