## 6. Days 30–60: Building Momentum

**Learning Objectives**

- [ ] Complete 1–2 medium-complexity tasks independently or semi-independently
- [ ] Own a sub-project or workstream and see it through
- [ ] Demonstrate that you understand your team's processes and can execute them reliably
- [ ] Build deeper product knowledge and understand how your role impacts customers

**Deliverables**

- [ ] Document a process or create a guide for something you've learned (helps solidify learning and helps future new hires)
- [ ] Propose one small improvement to a team process based on your fresh perspective
- [ ] Deliver 1–2 additional work items with minimal supervision

**Relationships**

- [ ] Continue 1:1s with your manager (weekly)
- [ ] Schedule deeper conversations with cross-functional partners about their priorities
- [ ] Attend a team outing, social event, or all-hands meeting if scheduled
- [ ] Help a fellow new hire if you've been here slightly longer

**Feedback and Check-In**

- [ ] Mid-point feedback from your manager: "You're now familiar with the role. Here's what I'm seeing..."
- [ ] Self-assessment: "I'm confident in these areas; I still need help with these."
- [ ] Identify one development goal for the next 30 days (new skill to learn, stretch project, mentoring relationship)

**30–60 Day Reflection**

- [ ] By day 50, schedule a progress review with your manager
- [ ] Discuss what's going well and what's challenging
- [ ] Align on priorities for the final 30 days of probation

---

## 7. Days 60–90: Demonstrating Competence

**Learning Objectives**

- [ ] Execute complex tasks with confidence and minimal supervision
- [ ] Proactively identify and solve problems
- [ ] Demonstrate embodiment of company values in how you work
- [ ] Build a strong reputation within your team and across the company

**Deliverables**

- [ ] Lead or co-own a meaningful workstream or project aligned with team OKRs
- [ ] Contribute ideas or solutions to team challenges
- [ ] Mentor or help on-board a new team member if applicable
- [ ] Document learnings and share with the team

**Relationships**

- [ ] You should feel comfortable approaching anyone in the company for help or advice
- [ ] Continue building relationships; these will be important for collaboration going forward
- [ ] Attend company events and participate in team culture actively

**90-Day Check-In and Probation Review**

- [ ] Schedule a formal 90-day probation review with your manager (and HR if applicable)
- [ ] Discuss performance against your initial goals and overall fit
- [ ] Confirmation of permanent employment status (standard for regular employees)
- [ ] Discussion of development plan for the next 6 months
- [ ] Celebrate your first 90 days!

