## 8. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)

**Q: Whom do I contact if my laptop or equipment has issues?**  
A: Reach out to the IT support team. The email (it@brightpath.com) or Slack channel (#it-support) will be in your welcome email. For urgent issues, call the office admin at the Bengaluru HQ. Response time is usually within 24 hours during business hours.

**Q: Where do I find the holiday list, leave policies, or other HR documents?**  
A: Log into the HR portal with your credentials (you'll receive access on Day 1). The Employee Handbook is also available as a PDF on your laptop and in the shared drive. For specific questions, contact HR at hr@brightpath.com.

**Q: What is the office dress code, and does it change for client meetings?**  
A: Standard office dress code is smart casual (collared shirts, trousers, closed-toe shoes). For client-facing meetings, we ask for more formal attire (blazers, formal trousers, professional dresses). Your manager will let you know if a specific meeting requires formal dress.

**Q: How long is my probation period?**  
A: The standard probation period is 3 months from your start date. During probation, your performance and cultural fit are evaluated. At the end of 3 months, you'll transition to permanent employment (usually without any change to role or compensation).

**Q: What does hybrid work mean, and how many office days am I expected to attend?**  
A: BrightPath operates a hybrid model. Bengaluru-based employees are expected in the office at least 2 days per week (usually Tuesday and Thursday, but this may vary by team). You can work from home on other days. Your manager will confirm the specific office days for your team.

**Q: Who is my buddy, and what do they do?**  
A: Your buddy is an experienced team member assigned to help you navigate informal questions, understand team culture, and provide peer support. They're not formally responsible for your training, but they're a friendly resource. Grab coffee or lunch with them to build the relationship!

**Q: How do I request leave or time off?**  
A: Use the HR portal to request leave. For planned leave, submit at least 3 working days in advance. For emergencies (sick leave, urgent personal matters), you can request the same day, but manager approval is still required. The first time you do this, your manager or buddy can walk you through.

**Q: What learning resources or courses are available?**  
A: Each employee gets an annual learning budget of INR 40,000 for courses, books, certifications, or conferences. Talk to your manager about what would be valuable for your role. Approval is usually quick if the learning is relevant.

**Q: What if I'm not sure how to do something or I'm confused?**  
A: Ask! This is normal, especially in the first 90 days. Ask your buddy, your manager, or anyone on the team. No question is too small. We believe asking for help is a sign of ownership, not weakness.

**Q: Will I be evaluated during my probation period?**  
A: Yes, informally during weekly 1:1s and formally at the 30-day, 60-day, and 90-day marks. The evaluation is about how you're learning, how you fit with the team, and whether you're meeting initial goals. It's a two-way conversation, not a judgment.

**Q: What happens if I need to work from home during probation?**  
A: Communicate with your manager. For occasional work-from-home days, there's no formal approval needed if your team supports hybrid work. For longer arrangements, discuss with your manager.

**Q: What is the company's policy on feedback?**  
A: We believe in frequent, direct, and respectful feedback. Your manager will give you feedback regularly, not just during formal reviews. You're also encouraged to ask for feedback from your manager and peers anytime. We see feedback as a gift, not a threat.

